          answer: 'Cervical fusion has excellent success rates of 85-95% for relieving arm pain and neurological symptoms. The fusion success rate (vertebrae successfully fusing together) exceeds 95% at our center. Most patients experience significant improvement in quality of life and can return to normal activities within 3-6 months. Success is highest when surgery is performed before severe permanent nerve damage occurs.'
